        "lastModified": "2026-06-17T10:58:01.490",
        "vulnStatus": "Deferred",
        "descriptions": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "value": "Perry before 0.5.1166 contains a JWT validation vulnerability that allows remote attackers to bypass token expiration by exploiting the unconditional setting of validate_exp = false in the verify_decode helper within the stdlib JWT verification path. Attackers in possession of a previously issued bearer token can present expired tokens to any jwt.verify() call and retain authenticated access indefinitely, bypassing force-expired sessions such as user logout or administrative revocation."
          }
        ],
